  "measurement_scope": "Regular per-day observation grid across the entire simulated interval, not continuous per-second telemetry. Daily batch ingestion and explicit daily retention; final advance adds 12h34m of covered idle time. Final retention is explicitly reported per case; zero means forever. Input-to-snapshot ratios with finite expiry include deliberately expired input and must not be described as aggregation-only savings. Input bytes/hash are actual NDJSON written outside the engine directory. Snapshots include metadata/indexes. Apparent file sizes are sampled every 10ms and after original ingestion/advancement/export/copy/close operations: directory scans are non-atomic and may miss transients or combine file lengths from different instants, so maxima are approximate and not physical allocation or guaranteed disk requirements. Working/export includes live database, sidecars, snapshot and copied file; source/reference disk and memory and SQLite temp files outside that directory are excluded. Engine phase timings exclude generation/reference evaluation; total case includes them. Shared execution environment; these measurements do not predict production throughput. KLL points vary across merges/runs; one stored sketch is compared identically after restart/copy. Rank regression checks use four times the empirical model plus 1/N, not a deterministic 99% guarantee."
